    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/9716XwAQM3U7h4LULDXU-.png) ⟨28⟩\nfabsssss⟨28⟩\n/\nuk-property-market-indicators⟨29⟩\nlike 0\nModalities:  Text ⟨30⟩\nFormats:  json ⟨31⟩\nLanguages:  English ⟨32⟩\nSize:  < 1K ⟨33⟩\nTags:  uk-government ⟨34⟩ housing ⟨35⟩ land-registry ⟨36⟩ open-data ⟨37⟩\nLibraries:  Datasets ⟨38⟩ pandas ⟨39⟩ Polars ⟨40⟩ + 1\nLicense:\nogl-v3\n Dataset card ⟨29⟩ Data Studio ⟨41⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨42⟩ Community 1 ⟨43⟩\nDataset Viewer\n Auto-converted to Parquet⟨44⟩ API Embed  Duplicate⟨45⟩ Data Studio\nSubset (1)\ndefault · 1 rows\ndefault (1 rows)\nSplit (1)\ntrain · 1 rows\ntrain (1 rows)\nSQL\nConsole  \n|  meta dict  |  indicators list  |  \n| --- | --- |  \n|  { \"source\": \"HM Land Registry Price Paid Data\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.gov.uk/government/statistical-data-sets/price-paid-data-downloads\", \"licence\": \"Open Government Licence v3.0\", \"attribution\": \"Contains HM Land Registry data (c) Crown copyright and database right 2026.\", \"year\": \"2025\", \"ppd_categor...  |  [ { \"local_authority\": \"ADUR\", \"county\": \"WEST SUSSEX\", \"year\": \"2025\", \"transactions\": 904, \"median_price\": 375000, \"lower_quartile_price\": 300000, \"upper_quartile_price\": 471937, \"mean_price\": 403000, \"new_build_share\": 0.0387, \"leasehold_share\": 0.2113, \"property_type_mi...  |  \n  * Method, and what the numbers are not⟨46⟩\n  * Files⟨47⟩\n  * Reproduce⟨48⟩\n  * Attribution⟨49⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨50⟩ UK Local-Authority Property-Market Indicators \nOpen, reproducible residential property-market indicators for every local authority in England and Wales, derived from HM Land Registry Price Paid Data.\nOne record per local-authority district: transaction volume, median and quartile prices, mean price, new-build share, leasehold share and property-type mix, for the 2025 calendar year.  \n|   |   |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| Local authorities  | **318**  |  \n| Standard transactions counted  | **760,607**  |  \n| Source  | HM Land Registry Price Paid Data (2025)  |  \n| Licence  | Open Government Licence v3.0  |  \n##   ⟨46⟩ Method, and what the numbers are not \nOnly **standard price-paid transactions** (PPD category A) are counted, so the figures exclude repossessions, buy-to-let portfolio transfers and other non-market or bulk sales. This is therefore a market **activity** indicator set (what sold, and for how much, in the open market this year) and explicitly _not_ a dwelling-stock census: it says nothing about homes that did not transact. Local authority is taken from the Price Paid `district` field, so no external postcode lookup is needed and every transaction with a district is attributed.\n##   ⟨47⟩ Files \n  * `data/la_property_indicators.json` — full indicators incl. property-type mix\n  * `data/la_property_indicators.csv` — flat table\n  * `scripts/build_indicators.py` — reproducible build from the raw Price Paid CSV\n\n\n##   ⟨48⟩ Reproduce \n\n```\ncurl -L -o data/pp-2025.csv \\\n  \"http://prod.publicdata.landregistry.gov.uk.s3-website-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/pp-2025.csv\"\npython3 scripts/build_indicators.py\n\n```\n\n##   ⟨49⟩ Attribution \nContains HM Land Registry data © Crown copyright and database right 2026. This information is licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0. An independent, self-initiated open dataset by Tesseract Academy⟨51⟩; not endorsed by HM Land Registry.\nCopy to bucket new\nUse this dataset \n\nDownloads last month\n    46\nNumber of rows: 1 Total file size: 193 kB\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨52⟩ Privacy⟨53⟩ About⟨54⟩ Careers⟨55⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
